# PWA-FOUNDATION-1 — PWA Foundation Rules

Durable contract: `docs/architecture/pwa-foundation.md`.

1. DaengtisiaMS uses PWA as an **additive web layer**. Removing it must leave a
   fully functional server-rendered application behind.
2. Laravel / Blade / Tailwind / Alpine / Vite remains the canonical frontend
   architecture.
3. Do **not** introduce React, Vue, Next.js, Nuxt, an SPA rewrite, or any new
   frontend framework, bundler plugin or PWA library (no Workbox,
   no `vite-plugin-pwa`). No business logic in JavaScript or the service worker.
4. The service worker may cache **only** safe static assets, via the
   `PWA-CACHE-ALLOWLIST` block in `public/sw.js`: prefixes `/build/`, `/pwa/`,
   `/assets/brand/` and the exact paths `/offline.html`,
   `/manifest.webmanifest`, `/favicon.ico`.
5. Never cache patient, RME, medical record, odontogram, consent, prescription,
   invoice, payment, receivable, report, export, dashboard or any authenticated
   response — including authenticated HTML, APIs, login, logout, session and
   CSRF endpoints. Navigations are network-first and their responses are never
   written to any cache.
6. Clinical operations stay **online-only**. Offline clinical data is a separate
   approved programme, never a side effect of PWA work.
7. Never store clinical data in Cache Storage, IndexedDB or `localStorage`
   through the PWA layer, and never queue a clinical write for later sync.
8. The manifest, icons and service-worker lifecycle are production foundation.
   Do not delete or rename them casually; `/sw.js` must stay at the document
   root or it loses root scope.
9. Every service-worker change must consider **cache versioning** and
   **stale-cache cleanup**: bump `CACHE_VERSION`, and purge only caches whose
   key starts with `daengtisiams-`. `cache.put()` must remain reachable from
   exactly one helper (`putIfAllowed`), which re-checks the allowlist. Do not
   add `skipWaiting()` — a release must never swap assets under a live form.
10. The PWA foundation is **not** doctor device authentication. An installed PWA
    proves nothing about which device is running it.
11. WebAuthn, passkeys and device restriction are a separate phase. Do not
    couple them to this layer.
12. PWA changes must preserve existing RBAC, policies, `BranchContext`, the room
    gate, authentication, `DoctorDeviceAuthorization` semantics, device
    enforcement flags and the RME workflow. PWA-FOUNDATION-1 is
    security-neutral with respect to authentication; keep it that way.
13. Every PWA change needs build + test + regression verification:
    `npm run build`, `npm run test:js`, `php artisan test tests/Feature/Pwa`.
    `tests/Feature/Pwa/PwaServiceWorkerCachePolicyTest.php` is a declared
    mandatory critical-gate suite in `config/ci_runner.php`; a rename must move
    that declaration, never drop it.
14. Source invariants are claims about **code**, not prose. The worker documents
    the APIs it must not call, so scans strip comments first — do not "fix" a
    scan by deleting the documentation.
